      "text": "FROM STATE INTEGRALS TO q-SERIES — It is well-known to the experts that multi-dimensional state integrals of prod- ucts of Faddeev’s quantum dilogarithm which arise in Quantum Topology can be written\n\n**FROM STATE INTEGRALS TO q-SERIES**\n\n*STAVROS GAROUFALIDIS AND RINAT KASHAEV*\n\n16 pp, 15 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** It is well-known to the experts that multi-dimensional state integrals of prod- ucts of Faddeev’s quantum dilogarithm which arise in Quantum Topology can be written as ﬁnite sums of products of basic hypergeometric series in q =e2πiτ and ˜q =e−2πi/τ . We illustrate this fact by giving a detailed proof for a family of one-dimensional integrals which includes state-integral invariants of 4 1 and 52 knots.\n\n**Outline.** 1 Introduction; 1.1 State-integrals and their q-series; 1.3 The case of the 41 knot; 1.4 The case of the 52 knot; 2 Proofs; 2.1 A residue computation; 2.4 Proof of Theorem 1.1; 2.5 Some auxiliary power series; 2.6 Proof of Proposition 2.2; 2.7 Proof of Lemma 1.5; 3 An application: state-integrals of the 41 an; 3.1 Proof of Corollary 1.7; 3.2 Proof of Corollary 1.8; Acknowledgments; References\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Corollary 1.6: (a) If we deﬁneω(q,x ) =FA,B(q,qx )/FA,B(q,x ) andω(q,x )n =∏n\n- Lemma 2.6: For part (b), we will use the series",
